.TH QUADRF-DATA 1 "October 2026" "QuadRF" "QuadRF"
.SH NAME
quadrf-data \- 802.11 OFDM Link transceiver and web HUD over the QuadRF radio
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B quadrf-data
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs an IEEE 802.11a OFDM PHY and Stop-and-Wait ARQ MAC on the QuadRF tile,
bridging IPv4 traffic through a Linux TUN interface (\fItun0\fR) and serving a
real-time browser HUD and WebSocket telemetry stream on port 8092 (proxied at
.IR /data/ ).
Two units on the same carrier frequency form a point-to-point IP link and peer
chat channel with a default TUN subnet of 10.99.0.0/24 derived from
.I QUADRF_HOSTNAME
in
.IR /etc/quadrf/quadrf.conf .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --port " port"
Web HUD and WebSocket listen port (default: 8092).
.TP
.BI --web-dir " path"
Static web assets directory (default: \fI/usr/share/quadrf-data/web\fR).
.TP
.B --gui
Start \fBquadrf-data.service\fR via \fBquadrf-app\fR and open \fI/data/\fR in
the operator browser.
.TP
.BI --tun " name"
Linux TUN interface name (default: \fItun0\fR).
.TP
.BI --ip " cidr"
TUN IPv4 address with prefix length (default: auto from hostname).
.TP
.BI --freq " MHz"
RF center frequency in MHz (default: 5860.0).
.TP
.BI --rate " name"
TX modulation rate in Mb/s (6, 9, 12, 18, 24, 36, 48, 54).
.TP
.BI --tx-gain " dB"
Transmit gain in dB (0..40, default: 34.0).
.TP
.BI --rx-gain " dB"
Receive gain in dB (0..63, default: 30.0).
.TP
.BI --tx-ant " mask"
Transmit antenna bitmask (1..15, default: 0x01).
.TP
.BI --rx-ant " mask"
Receive antenna bitmask (1..15, default: 0x01).
.TP
.B --pa-mute
Mute SE5003L PA during receive and unmute around DSI VSYNC burst scanout (default).
.TP
.B --no-pa-mute
Keep PA unmuted continuously.
.TP
.B --smoke-test
Run offline synthetic DSP loopback validation across all 802.11a rates.
.TP
.BR --help ", " -h
List command-line options.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR quadrf-jtag (1),
.BR quadrf-psd (1),
.BR quadrf-app (8)
